node_modules/
dist/
out/
scratch/
*.log
.DS_Store
.superpowers/

# What electron-builder writes: the unpacked app and the installer. Built from
# what is in here, so it belongs to nobody's history.
release/

# Where every harness puts its screenshots, probe assets and measurements
# (test/harness/shots.js, tiles-shots.js, gradient-shots.js, walkthrough.js all
# default into it). Evidence for whoever is looking at the app today, made again
# by re-running the harness, and 78 MB of it — one `git add -A` away from being
# in the history for ever. Nothing in it is tracked, which was checked before
# this line was written.
work/

# Working notes that belong to this machine, not to the project.
#
# SNAPSHOT.md is the handover note between working sessions — where the work
# stands, what to pick up next, which files somebody else is holding right now.
# It is written for whoever continues the work here and reads as noise to
# anybody who arrives at the repository, so it stays on disk and out of the
# history. The build plans it refers to live in .superpowers/, ignored above
# for the same reason: they are instructions to the workers, not documentation
# of the program.
SNAPSHOT.md
